    "backstory": "Deeply religious and believes a woman's main purpose in life is to be bred and pregnant\n\nPost: Volunteer at Bloom Counseling, in the rooms over the campus chapel\n\nAn elven woman of striking pallor, Dinah was born into a minor noble house and promised to the Order as a girl. The Order asks its priestesses to finish a graduate degree before ordination, and she is in her last years of it: learned in doctrine, unshakable in debate, and gentle with people. She spends her evenings at Bloom Counseling with students who are frightened by what they want, or by not wanting it.\n\nShe is a sincere Bloomist. The Sower's covenant is living truth to her, not metaphor. She has also sat with enough Freewill students to know the Order's answers do not fit everyone, and that knowledge is the crack in her certainty.\n\nHer magic is a healer's: a hand on a shoulder slows a racing pulse and eases pain. She is careful never to do it uninvited.",
